  "evidence": "Original N/E/U shows a sustained negative shift in N and E (and positive U) beginning around index 448, persisting through ~486–489, with clear return toward pre-event levels by index 490–492. The interior of both P1 (447–486) and P2 (448–489) contains coherent motion without abrupt internal steps, but P2 extends slightly longer and better captures the full return onset (index 489 aligns with first post-offset recovery point). However, the offset is not perfectly closed: post-return N/E remain ~1–2 mm offset from pre-event baseline, consistent with an independent permanent step occurring during or after the temporary platform. Since only one genuine temporary platform is supported by the observations—and P2 more accurately brackets the observed shift-and-return—P1 is redundant and overlapping. Replace with P2 only.",
  "pair_ids": ["P2"]
}
